• Live transcription of long dictations: speech is transcribed in fragments as you go, cut at natural pauses and joined into clean text.
• Much more memory-efficient — recording memory no longer grows with dictation length, so very long sessions can't exhaust the device.
• After a successful send, the voice keyboard now switches back to your typing keyboard automatically.
• A paused dictation opened on a different text field starts fresh — the old transcript stays in the clipboard.
